       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose appears to be an error.\n\n- **Daily total:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose for immediate-release metformin is 2550 mg/day, and extended-release is 2000 mg/day.\n- **Tablet strength:** Metformin is not commonly available as 1700 mg. Standard strengths are 500, 850, and 1000 mg.\n\nThis may be a typo or a confusion with another strength. Common options would be:\n\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the labeled maximum for IR)\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals** (1500 mg/day)\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2000 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg TID is what you intend, please confirm that too, and I'll note the reason on the order. Since the patient has normal kidney function, renal dose limits are not the concern here."
