      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered this order. Even with your confirmation, 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day, about twice the labeled maximum of 2550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis, and 1700 mg isn't a standard tablet strength, so the order could be dispensed incorrectly.\n\nPlease check the dose with the prescriber or pharmacy before I enter it. If the intended dose is one of these, tell me and I'll enter it right away:\n\n- Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals (2550 mg/day)\n- Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals (1500 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO BID with meals (2000 mg/day)\n\nIf the prescriber confirms that a dose above the labeled maximum is intended, the pharmacist will need to review it before it's dispensed. I can enter it with a note saying so, but I'd want that verification to happen first."
      }
